      "id": 478939,
      "username": "TalhaButt2508",
      "name": "Talha Butt2508",
      "created_at": "2025-08-26T06:50:10.871Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi if anyone faces similar issue, Solution:<br>\nIf in between the fiscal year, you’re implementing and do a equalized division in monthly distribution, and test it by posting the expense more than the distributed % for a specific month it wont be trigerred as the months before that do have 100% budget left so is adjusted.<br>\nTo test it, simply divide Total Budget <strong>by</strong> Current + Remaining Months of the year then allocate the resultant for current and remaining months and months before current for them keep distribution ZERO. Now test the trigger of stop by making a posting exceeding the monthly accumularted allowance.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/0/7/07af9ff1d6c7f9e66cb56cdfd582a42d5f70e674.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/07af9ff1d6c7f9e66cb56cdfd582a42d5f70e674\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/7/07af9ff1d6c7f9e66cb56cdfd582a42d5f70e674_2_690x390.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"15ZCeqHXigtKgFNUSKhbFlMfv9y\" width=\"690\" height=\"390\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/7/07af9ff1d6c7f9e66cb56cdfd582a42d5f70e674_2_690x390.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/0/7/07af9ff1d6c7f9e66cb56cdfd582a42d5f70e674.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/0/7/07af9ff1d6c7f9e66cb56cdfd582a42d5f70e674.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"FCFCFC\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1009×571 23.3 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
